      "content": "Yes, duct work can be designed poorly or have an incorrect static pressure rating within Phoenix's extreme temperatures, causing air to get trapped upstream before reaching that room. There is also a remote possibility of a foreign object inside the ducts obstructing flow, though water damage or mold buildup in inaccessible wall cavities is the most likely culprit. Since HVAC repairs under warranty are often free for the tenant if caused by improper installation or warm air failure, verify if their service contract covers these hidden investigations.",
